      "schema:name": "dilations-nearer-neurons-than-constrictions",
      "schema:description": "Following ChR2 optogenetic activation at 458 nm, capillary dilations occur on average 16.1±14.3 µm from the nearest labeled pyramidal neuron while constrictions occur 21.9±14.6 µm away (4.3 mW/mm²; p<1e-4), and this spatial segregation is absent under control 552 nm illumination.",
